Mei: Yes! I want to learn about global business and improve my English.
Tom: That''s great. But aren''t you worried about the cost?
Mei: A little. Tuition and living expenses are high, so I made a careful budget.
Tom: Smart. Will you live in a dormitory or with a host family?
Mei: A host family. They can help me adapt and comfort me when I miss home.
Tom: Good idea. What''s your biggest goal for the year?
Mei: To set up my own business in China one day. This is the first step.', 'Tom 听说梅报名了去英国的交换项目;梅想学全球商业并提高英语;Tom 担心费用;梅说学费生活费高,所以做了仔细的预算;她选住寄宿家庭,能帮她适应、想家时给安慰;她最大的目标是将来在中国创业,这是第一步。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why did Mei sign up for the exchange programme?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To learn about global business and improve her English.","To avoid studying at home.","To stop learning English.","To travel for fun only."]},{"q":"What is Tom worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The weather in the UK.","The cost of studying abroad.","Mei''s English level.","The food on the plane."]},{"q":"How did Mei deal with the high expenses?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She made a careful budget.","She borrowed money from Tom.","She gave up the programme.","She ignored the problem."]},{"q":"Why does Mei choose a host family?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Because it is free.","Because they can help her adapt and comfort her.","Because the school requires it.","Because dormitories are full."]},{"q":"What is Mei''s biggest goal for the year?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To stay in the UK forever.","To become a tour guide.","To start her own business in China one day.","To learn French as well."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2');
They hope to gain a global perspective and improve their general competence.
However, studying overseas can also bring tremendous pressure.
Some students suffer from culture shock in unfamiliar surroundings.
With careful planning, though, the experience can change them for the better.', '近年来,越来越多的年轻人选择出国留学;他们希望获得全球视野、提升综合能力;然而出国也会带来巨大压力;一些学生在陌生环境中遭遇文化冲击;不过若计划周全,这段经历能让他们变得更好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is happening with young people and studying abroad?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Fewer of them want to study at all.","None of them go overseas now.","They only study at home.","More and more of them choose to study abroad."]},{"q":"What do these students hope to gain?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A global perspective and better competence.","A free holiday.","An easier life with no work.","More money from their schools."]},{"q":"What problem can studying overseas bring?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No homework at all.","Tremendous pressure.","Too much free time.","Better weather."]},{"q":"What do some students suffer from in new surroundings?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A bad memory.","A loss of money.","Culture shock.","A fear of flying."]},{"q":"What can make the experience change them for the better?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Avoiding all locals.","Staying in their rooms.","Refusing to learn the language.","Careful planning."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2');
Aisha: Thank you. It''s a pleasure to be here.
Host: What made you feel close to your teacher, Ms Hu?
Aisha: She often invited us to her home for meals, so I felt like family.
Host: Lovely. Why did you decide to become a teacher yourself?
Aisha: I wanted to share that same warmth with new learners of Chinese.
Host: And why do your students see Chinese as useful?
Aisha: Because more jobs now need people who can connect China with the world.', '主持人欢迎 Aisha 并感谢她到来;Aisha 表示很高兴;主持人问是什么让她与胡老师亲近;Aisha 说老师常请他们到家里吃饭,让她有家的感觉;她想把同样的温暖分享给新的中文学习者;她的学生认为中文有用,因为越来越多的工作需要能连接中国与世界的人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What made Aisha feel like part of Ms Hu''s family?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The invitations to home-cooked meals.","The high marks she earned.","The free books she got.","The large classroom."]},{"q":"Why did Aisha become a teacher?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To earn a high salary.","To share the same warmth with new learners.","To leave her country.","To stop teaching Chinese."]},{"q":"Why do her students think Chinese is useful?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because it has no grammar.","Because it is easy to write.","Because more jobs need people who connect China with the world.","Because it replaces English."]},{"q":"How does the host begin the interview?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By asking about the weather.","By telling a long story.","By saying goodbye.","By welcoming Aisha and thanking her."]},{"q":"How does Aisha describe her feeling at Ms Hu''s home?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She felt like family.","She felt bored.","She felt afraid.","She felt unwelcome."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2');
English is a stress-based language, so some words are not stressed.
Small words like pronouns and prepositions often use a weak form.
For example, in ''Are you ready?'', ''are'' and ''you'' sound very light.
If you learn the weak forms, you will understand native speakers more easily.', '给觉得快速英语难懂的学习者一个有用的小贴士:英语是重音语言,有些词不重读;代词、介词等小词常用弱读形式;例如在“Are you ready?”中,are 和 you 读得很轻;学会弱读形式,你就能更容易听懂母语者。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only teachers of Chinese.","Learners who find fast English hard to follow.","Only native speakers.","People who never listen to English."]},{"q":"What kind of language is English, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A picture-based language.","A language with no rules.","A stress-based language.","A silent language."]},{"q":"Which words often use a weak form?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Long and rare words.","Names of people.","Numbers only.","Small words like pronouns and prepositions."]},{"q":"What happens to ''are'' and ''you'' in ''Are you ready?''","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They sound very light.","They are shouted loudly.","They are spelled differently.","They are left out."]},{"q":"What is the benefit of learning weak forms?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["You can stop studying English.","You understand native speakers more easily.","You will speak like a robot.","You will forget grammar."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2');
Anna: That''s normal at first. The best cure is to get involved in activities.
Liu: Really? I usually just stay in my room and study.
Anna: Try joining a club or a sports team. You''ll soon make new friends.
Liu: But my English isn''t perfect. I''m afraid of making mistakes.
Anna: Don''t worry about mistakes. Every one is a chance to learn.
Liu: That makes sense. I''ll be braver and speak up more.
Anna: Exactly. Step out of your comfort zone, and you''ll feel at home soon.', '刘来这里一个月仍觉得自己像局外人,向 Anna 求建议;Anna 说一开始很正常,最好的办法是参与活动;刘平时只待在房间里学习;Anna 建议加入社团或球队,很快会交到新朋友;刘担心英语不完美、怕犯错;Anna 说别担心犯错,每个错误都是学习的机会;刘决定更勇敢、多开口;Anna 鼓励他走出舒适区,很快就会有家的感觉。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How does Liu feel after a month abroad?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Completely at home.","Eager to leave at once.","Like an outsider.","Proud of his English."]},{"q":"What is Anna''s best piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To study alone all day.","To avoid all classmates.","To return home quickly.","To get involved in activities."]},{"q":"What does Liu usually do in his free time?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He stays in his room and studies.","He travels around the city.","He calls his family.","He joins many clubs."]},{"q":"What does Anna say about making mistakes?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They should never happen.","Every one is a chance to learn.","They mean he should quit.","They make him look foolish."]},{"q":"What does Liu decide to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To stop studying English.","To stay in his room longer.","To be braver and speak up more.","To go home immediately."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2');
You become a kind of cultural envoy for your homeland.
By sharing your food, music and stories, you help others understand it.
At the same time, you learn to see the world from new angles.
In this way, each student helps to build a bridge between nations.', '当你在另一个国家学习时,你做的不只是上课;你成了祖国的一种文化使者;通过分享你的食物、音乐和故事,你帮助别人理解它;与此同时,你学会从新的角度看世界;这样,每个学生都在为各国之间架起一座桥梁。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do you do besides attending classes when studying abroad?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["You forget your own country.","You stop meeting people.","You only take exams.","You become a cultural envoy for your homeland."]},{"q":"How do you help others understand your homeland?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By sharing your food, music and stories.","By keeping everything secret.","By staying silent.","By copying their culture."]},{"q":"What do you learn to do at the same time?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To dislike other cultures.","To see the world from new angles.","To stop studying.","To travel less."]},{"q":"What does each student help to build, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A bigger house.","A faster train.","A bridge between nations.","A larger school."]},{"q":"What is the main message of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Studying abroad is a waste of time.","Students should never share their culture.","Only teachers can be cultural envoys.","Studying abroad can make you a bridge between cultures."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2');

